expression: text
---
── section · review ──
  channel          team  {row:0}
  user group       @review-squad  {row:1}
> template         {group} :gitlab: {mrs}  [Review please {group}: {mrs}|]  {row:2}
  link text        mr  {row:3}
  each request     {link} {title}  {row:4}
  test channel     try  {row:5}
  ask again        after 2 working days without a reply  {row:6}
── detail · template ──
AS YOU TYPE
:run_passed: mentions the group picked under user group (in the review channel); posts: Review please <!subteam^S0REVIEW01>: <https://git.example/acme/team-a/api/-/merge_requests/263|mr> Add a stats endpoint for the dashboard

The message: {mrs} is each merge request as written under each request, or one bullet each for several; {count} is how many. {group} mentions the user group picked above, and {@handle} any of Slack's user groups by its handle. Both are sent as Slack's mention of the group's id, so it pings, and only in the review channel. The placeholders of each request work here too; with several merge requests each is their different values joined by commas. :name: is an emoji.

ACCEPTS
text with {mrs} or {link}; {count}, {group}, {@handle}, {link}, {url}, {repo}, {project}, {iid}, {title}, {branch}, {target}, {author}, {tickets} optional

NOW
{group} :gitlab: {mrs}

WITH A SAMPLE MERGE REQUEST
Review please @review-squad: mr <https://git.example/acme/team-a/api/-/merge_requests/263> Add a stats endpoint for the dashboard

WITH TWO
Review please @review-squad:
• api !263 <https://git.example/acme/team-a/api/-/merge_requests/263> Add a stats endpoint for the dashboard
• web !12 <https://git.example/acme/team-a/web/-/merge_requests/12> Show the stats

config: [slack.review] template
